The middleware above is a solid foundation. In enterprise applications, we often extend it by:

Checking that the Authorization header starts with Bearer .
Handling malformed headers more gracefully.
Logging authentication failures.
Adding role-based authorization (e.g., admin, customer) after the JWT is verified.
Moving protected routes into separate route files instead of defining them all in server.js.
